{
  "title": "5 Ways to Get Rich on a Normal Salary",
  "thumbnail": "NO LUCK NEEDED",
  "hook_formula": "The Mistake",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "chapter": "Why you're broke again",
      "set": "room",
      "lines": [
        {
          "key": "paycheck",
          "text": "Your paycheck lands, and three weeks later, you're broke again.",
          "expr": "o",
          "holding": "dollar-banknote",
          "camera": "wide",
          "beat": {
            "type": "tags",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "RENT",
                "icon": "house"
              },
              {
                "text": "GROCERIES",
                "icon": "shopping-cart"
              },
              {
                "text": "SUBSCRIPTIONS",
                "icon": "mobile-phone"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "salary",
          "text": "Stop blaming your salary.",
          "expr": "smug",
          "beat": {
            "type": "stamp",
            "text": "IT'S NOT YOUR SALARY"
          },
          "holding": ""
        },
        {
          "key": "five",
          "text": "It's five moves nobody showed you, and almost none of them cost a cent.",
          "expr": "grin",
          "emote": "idea",
          "beat": {
            "type": "steps",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "SAVE",
                "icon": "money-bag"
              },
              {
                "text": "NO DEBT",
                "icon": "credit-card"
              },
              {
                "text": "INVEST",
                "icon": "chart-increasing"
              },
              {
                "text": "EARN",
                "icon": "briefcase"
              },
              {
                "text": "OWN",
                "icon": "house-with-garden"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "turn",
          "text": "By the end of this video, you'll have a simple machine that builds wealth on autopilot.",
          "expr": "grin",
          "beat": {
            "type": "icon",
            "icons": [
              "gear",
              "money-bag"
            ],
            "label": "YOUR MONEY MACHINE"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "disclaimer",
          "text": "Quick note. I'm a stick figure, not a financial advisor. This is education, not advice.",
          "expr": "smug",
          "camera": "stick",
          "beat": {
            "type": "icon",
            "icon": "graduation-cap",
            "label": "EDUCATION, NOT ADVICE"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "way1",
      "chapter": "1. Pay yourself first",
      "set": "kitchen",
      "lines": [
        {
          "key": "title",
          "text": "Move one. Pay yourself first.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "title",
            "n": 1,
            "title": "PAY YOURSELF FIRST",
            "sub": "before anything else gets paid",
            "color": "green",
            "icon": "money-bag"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "most",
          "text": "Most people budget like this. Pay the rent, buy the food, have some fun, and save whatever is left.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "flow",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "RENT",
                "icon": "house"
              },
              {
                "text": "FOOD",
                "icon": "shopping-cart"
              },
              {
                "text": "FUN",
                "icon": "popcorn"
              },
              {
                "text": "SAVE?",
                "icon": "money-bag"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "nothing",
          "text": "The problem? There's almost never anything left.",
          "expr": "frown",
          "emote": "sweat",
          "beat": {
            "type": "counter",
            "from": 300,
            "to": 0,
            "prefix": "$",
            "label": "left to save",
            "color": "red",
            "icon": "money-with-wings"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "flip",
          "text": "So flip the order. The day your pay arrives, a fixed slice goes to savings first, automatically.",
          "expr": "grin",
          "emote": "idea",
          "beat": {
            "type": "flow",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "PAYDAY",
                "icon": "calendar"
              },
              {
                "text": "SAVE FIRST",
                "icon": "money-bag"
              },
              {
                "text": "BILLS",
                "icon": "receipt"
              },
              {
                "text": "LIFE",
                "icon": "pizza"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "rule",
          "text": "A popular starting point is the fifty thirty twenty rule. Fifty percent for needs, thirty for wants, and twenty for savings and paying off debt.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "donut",
            "title": "THE 50 / 30 / 20 RULE",
            "center": "YOUR PAY",
            "segments": [
              {
                "label": "NEEDS",
                "value": 50,
                "color": "blue",
                "icon": "house"
              },
              {
                "label": "WANTS",
                "value": 30,
                "color": "gold",
                "icon": "popcorn"
              },
              {
                "label": "SAVE",
                "value": 20,
                "color": "green",
                "icon": "money-bag"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "small",
          "text": "If twenty percent feels impossible, start with five. The habit matters more than the number. Then raise it every time your income goes up.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "timeline",
            "title": "GROW YOUR SLICE",
            "points": [
              {
                "label": "5%",
                "text": "start here",
                "icon": "seedling"
              },
              {
                "label": "10%",
                "text": "first raise",
                "icon": "chart-increasing"
              },
              {
                "label": "15%",
                "text": "next raise",
                "icon": "flexed-biceps-medium-light"
              },
              {
                "label": "20%+",
                "text": "the goal",
                "icon": "trophy"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "brain",
          "text": "Keep that money in a separate account you don't see every day. Out of sight, out of mind.",
          "emote": "think",
          "beat": {
            "type": "icon",
            "icons": [
              "bank",
              "locked"
            ],
            "label": "OUT OF SIGHT, OUT OF MIND"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "auto",
          "text": "Set it up once, and willpower never gets a vote.",
          "expr": "smug",
          "holding": "mobile-phone",
          "camera": "stick",
          "beat": {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "AUTOMATE IT",
            "sub": "set it once, forget it",
            "icon": "gear",
            "color": "green"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "way2",
      "chapter": "2. Kill high-interest debt",
      "set": "office",
      "lines": [
        {
          "key": "title",
          "text": "Move two. Kill high interest debt.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "title",
            "n": 2,
            "title": "KILL HIGH-INTEREST DEBT",
            "sub": "stop the leak first",
            "color": "red",
            "icon": "credit-card"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "bucket",
          "text": "Saving while you carry credit card debt is like filling a bucket with a hole in the bottom.",
          "expr": "worried",
          "holding": "",
          "beat": {
            "type": "prop",
            "name": "bucket",
            "label": "THE LEAKY BUCKET"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "rates",
          "text": "Credit cards often charge twenty percent a year or more. A savings account pays a small fraction of that.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "compare",
            "left": {
              "title": "YOUR CARD",
              "icon": "credit-card",
              "items": [
                "charges 20%+ a year"
              ],
              "color": "red"
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "YOUR SAVINGS",
              "icon": "bank",
              "items": [
                "earns a lot less"
              ],
              "color": "green"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "example",
          "text": "For example, three thousand dollars at twenty two percent costs you over seven hundred dollars in interest in a single year.",
          "expr": "o",
          "beat": {
            "type": "counter",
            "to": 700,
            "prefix": "$",
            "suffix": "+",
            "label": "in interest, in one year",
            "color": "red",
            "icon": "fire",
            "note": "example: $3,000 on a card at 22% a year"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "nothing",
          "text": "That's money you worked for, buying absolutely nothing.",
          "expr": "frown",
          "emote": "angry",
          "beat": {
            "type": "prop",
            "name": "monster"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "avalanche",
          "text": "The fastest way out is the avalanche method. Pay the minimum on everything, then throw every extra dollar at the highest interest rate.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "list",
            "title": "THE AVALANCHE METHOD",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "list every debt and its rate",
                "icon": "clipboard"
              },
              {
                "text": "pay every minimum",
                "icon": "check-mark-button"
              },
              {
                "text": "extra money: highest rate first",
                "icon": "fire"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "roll",
          "text": "When that one's gone, roll its payment into the next. Each debt dies faster than the last.",
          "expr": "grin",
          "beat": {
            "type": "flow",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "27% CARD",
                "icon": "credit-card"
              },
              {
                "text": "18% LOAN",
                "icon": "receipt"
              },
              {
                "text": "9% CAR",
                "icon": "automobile"
              },
              {
                "text": "DEBT FREE",
                "icon": "party-popper"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "choice",
          "text": "Prefer quick wins? The snowball method clears the smallest balance first. It can cost a little more, but the best plan is the one you stick with.",
          "burst": "confetti",
          "beat": {
            "type": "compare",
            "left": {
              "title": "AVALANCHE",
              "icon": "fire",
              "items": [
                "highest rate first",
                "saves the most"
              ],
              "color": "red"
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "SNOWBALL",
              "icon": "snowman",
              "items": [
                "smallest balance first",
                "quick wins"
              ],
              "color": "blue"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "emergency",
          "text": "And build an emergency fund, so one flat tire doesn't put you right back on the card. Many experts suggest working up to three to six months of expenses.",
          "emote": "idea",
          "beat": {
            "type": "cards",
            "items": [
              {
                "icon": "automobile",
                "title": "LIFE HAPPENS",
                "text": "flat tyres, vet bills, job changes",
                "color": "red"
              },
              {
                "icon": "shield",
                "title": "3-6 MONTHS",
                "text": "of expenses, saved over time",
                "color": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "way3",
      "chapter": "3. Invest early",
      "set": "board",
      "lines": [
        {
          "key": "title",
          "text": "Move three. Invest early, and let time do the heavy lifting.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "title",
            "n": 3,
            "title": "INVEST EARLY",
            "sub": "let time do the heavy lifting",
            "color": "blue",
            "icon": "seedling"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "compound",
          "text": "Compound growth means your money earns money, and then that money earns money too.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "flow",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "YOUR MONEY",
                "icon": "dollar-banknote"
              },
              {
                "text": "+ GROWTH",
                "icon": "seedling"
              },
              {
                "text": "+ GROWTH ON GROWTH",
                "icon": "deciduous-tree"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "rule72",
          "text": "Here's a handy shortcut called the rule of seventy two. Divide seventy two by your yearly return, and that's roughly how many years your money takes to double.",
          "emote": "idea",
          "beat": {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "72 / RETURN = YEARS TO DOUBLE",
            "sub": "example: at 8% a year, about 9 years",
            "icon": "hourglass-not-done",
            "color": "blue"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "me",
          "text": "Watch. I invest two hundred dollars a month, starting at twenty five. My friend Larry invests the exact same amount, but waits until he's thirty five.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "timeline",
            "title": "SAME $200 A MONTH",
            "points": [
              {
                "label": "25",
                "text": "I start",
                "icon": "seedling"
              },
              {
                "label": "35",
                "text": "Larry starts",
                "icon": "alarm-clock"
              },
              {
                "label": "65",
                "text": "we compare",
                "icon": "magnifying-glass-tilted-left"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "assume",
          "text": "To keep the math simple, let's assume seven percent a year on average. That's an assumption, not a promise. Real markets jump around.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "ASSUMED: 7% A YEAR",
            "sub": "not a promise: markets go up and down",
            "icon": "chart-increasing"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "chart",
          "text": "Here's how both pots grow. By sixty five, Larry has about two hundred and forty thousand dollars. I have about five hundred and twenty five thousand.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "chart",
            "title": "$200 A MONTH, ASSUMED 7% A YEAR",
            "x": [
              "25",
              "35",
              "45",
              "55",
              "65"
            ],
            "prefix": "$",
            "unit": "K",
            "series": [
              {
                "label": "ME",
                "values": [
                  0,
                  35,
                  104,
                  244,
                  525
                ],
                "color": "green"
              },
              {
                "label": "LARRY",
                "values": [
                  null,
                  0,
                  35,
                  104,
                  244
                ],
                "color": "blue"
              }
            ],
            "note": "example only: monthly contributions, 7% average yearly return, no fees or taxes"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "time",
          "text": "Same habit. Only ten extra years. More than double the money. The difference wasn't talent. It was time.",
          "expr": "grin",
          "burst": "sparkle",
          "beat": {
            "type": "stamp",
            "text": "THE DIFFERENCE WAS TIME",
            "color": "green"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "index",
          "text": "So where does that money go? Many people use low cost index funds. One fund holds hundreds of companies, so you're never betting everything on one.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "grid",
            "icon": "office-building",
            "count": 20,
            "highlight": 20,
            "label": "ONE FUND, HUNDREDS OF COMPANIES"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "match",
          "text": "And if your job offers a retirement match, take the full match first. It's the closest thing to free money you'll ever see.",
          "emote": "money",
          "beat": {
            "type": "cards",
            "items": [
              {
                "icon": "money-bag",
                "title": "YOU PUT IN",
                "text": "a slice of your pay",
                "color": "green"
              },
              {
                "icon": "handshake",
                "title": "THEY MATCH IT",
                "text": "up to their limit",
                "color": "gold"
              },
              {
                "icon": "gem-stone",
                "title": "FREE MONEY",
                "text": "don't leave it behind",
                "color": "blue"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "hold",
          "text": "Keep fees low, keep adding every month, and don't panic sell when the market drops. It will drop. Stay on the hill.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "list",
            "title": "THE INVESTING RULES",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "keep fees low",
                "icon": "magnifying-glass-tilted-left"
              },
              {
                "text": "keep adding every month",
                "icon": "calendar"
              },
              {
                "text": "don't panic sell",
                "icon": "shield"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "way4",
      "chapter": "4. Grow your income",
      "set": "office",
      "lines": [
        {
          "key": "title",
          "text": "Move four. Grow your income, then guard it.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "title",
            "n": 4,
            "title": "GROW YOUR INCOME",
            "sub": "then guard it",
            "color": "gold",
            "icon": "briefcase"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "floor",
          "text": "Cutting costs has a floor. You can only skip so many coffees. But earning has no ceiling.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "compare",
            "left": {
              "title": "CUTTING COSTS",
              "icon": "hot-beverage",
              "items": [
                "has a floor"
              ],
              "color": "red"
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "EARNING MORE",
              "icon": "rocket",
              "items": [
                "has no ceiling"
              ],
              "color": "green"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "skill",
          "text": "The best investment is usually you. A skill people will pay for compounds just like money does.",
          "emote": "idea",
          "beat": {
            "type": "icon",
            "icons": [
              "books",
              "light-bulb",
              "graduation-cap"
            ],
            "label": "INVEST IN YOUR SKILLS"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "tenmin",
          "text": "Even ten minutes of practice a day adds up to more than sixty hours a year.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "counter",
            "to": 60,
            "suffix": "+ HOURS",
            "label": "ten minutes a day, for one year",
            "icon": "alarm-clock",
            "color": "blue"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "use",
          "text": "Then cash it in. Ask for a raise and bring proof of your results. Switch jobs if yours won't pay what you're worth. Or start something on the side.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "cards",
            "items": [
              {
                "icon": "chart-increasing",
                "title": "ASK",
                "text": "for a raise, with proof",
                "color": "green"
              },
              {
                "icon": "briefcase",
                "title": "SWITCH",
                "text": "to a job that pays more",
                "color": "blue"
              },
              {
                "icon": "laptop",
                "title": "BUILD",
                "text": "something on the side",
                "color": "gold"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "trap",
          "text": "But watch out for lifestyle creep. When income goes up, spending sneaks up right behind it.",
          "expr": "worried",
          "emote": "sweat",
          "beat": {
            "type": "icon",
            "icons": [
              "television",
              "automobile",
              "shopping-bags"
            ],
            "label": "LIFESTYLE CREEP",
            "sub": "bigger pay, bigger bills, same savings"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "half",
          "text": "A simple rule. When you get a raise, save at least half of it. Live a little better, not a lot better.",
          "expr": "grin",
          "beat": {
            "type": "donut",
            "title": "EVERY RAISE",
            "center": "RAISE",
            "segments": [
              {
                "label": "SAVE & INVEST",
                "value": 50,
                "color": "green",
                "icon": "money-bag"
              },
              {
                "label": "ENJOY",
                "value": 50,
                "color": "gold",
                "icon": "party-popper"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "way5",
      "chapter": "5. Own things that earn",
      "set": "park",
      "lines": [
        {
          "key": "title",
          "text": "Move five. Own things that earn while you sleep.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "title",
            "n": 5,
            "title": "OWN THINGS THAT EARN",
            "sub": "while you sleep",
            "color": "green",
            "icon": "house-with-garden"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "two",
          "text": "There are two kinds of stuff. Things that take money out of your pocket, and things that put money in.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "compare",
            "left": {
              "title": "TAKES MONEY",
              "icon": "automobile",
              "items": [
                "new cars",
                "gadgets",
                "subscriptions"
              ],
              "color": "red"
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "MAKES MONEY",
              "icon": "house-with-garden",
              "items": [
                "index funds",
                "a business",
                "rental property"
              ],
              "color": "green"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "assets",
          "text": "Shares in companies, a small business, a rental, or things you create that keep selling. Those can pay you again and again.",
          "beat": {
            "type": "cards",
            "items": [
              {
                "icon": "chart-increasing",
                "title": "SHARES",
                "text": "own part of companies",
                "color": "green"
              },
              {
                "icon": "convenience-store",
                "title": "BUSINESS",
                "text": "earns while you're away",
                "color": "blue"
              },
              {
                "icon": "open-book",
                "title": "CREATIONS",
                "text": "make once, sell forever",
                "color": "gold"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "hours",
          "text": "Your job trades hours for money, and there are only so many hours in a day.",
          "expr": "flat",
          "beat": {
            "type": "flow",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "1 HOUR",
                "icon": "stopwatch"
              },
              {
                "text": "1 PAYCHECK",
                "icon": "dollar-banknote"
              },
              {
                "text": "NO HOURS LEFT",
                "icon": "sleeping-face"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "break",
          "text": "Owning things breaks that link. That's how your money starts working while you sleep.",
          "emote": "zzz",
          "burst": "coins",
          "beat": {
            "type": "icon",
            "icons": [
              "sleeping-face",
              "money-bag"
            ],
            "label": "MONEY WHILE YOU SLEEP"
          }
        },
        {
          "key": "small",
          "text": "Start small. One share of an index fund, or one thing you build on a weekend.",
          "expr": "grin",
          "beat": {
            "type": "cards",
            "items": [
              {
                "icon": "chart-increasing",
                "title": "ONE SHARE",
                "text": "of an index fund",
                "color": "green"
              },
              {
                "icon": "hammer",
                "title": "ONE PROJECT",
                "text": "built on a weekend",
                "color": "gold"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "machine",
      "chapter": "The whole machine",
      "set": "stage",
      "lines": [
        {
          "key": "intro",
          "text": "So here's the machine. Pay yourself first, so money exists. Kill the debt, so nothing leaks. Invest it, so it grows. Grow your income, so there's more to feed in. And own things that earn, so it keeps going without you.",
          "expr": "grin",
          "beat": {
            "type": "steps",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "SAVE",
                "icon": "money-bag"
              },
              {
                "text": "NO DEBT",
                "icon": "credit-card"
              },
              {
